=== entry 959714ba4fcc
kind: translation
rules: todolist
intent: Opens the visible phase list in T3's terms (update_plan in Codex, the reply in Claude Code) and keeps it current. Preserve the six phase names and that it opens before launching anything.
--- upstream
Open a todolist with one entry per phase (Frame, Fan out, Cross-judge, Pick, Graft, Verify) before launching anything.
--- patched
Open a step list with one entry per phase (Frame, Fan out, Cross-judge, Pick, Graft, Verify) before launching anything, and keep it current at each phase. Codex keeps it with `update_plan`. Claude Code keeps it in the reply.

=== entry e31c37c35e68
kind: translation
rules: model-role, model-effort, general-purpose
intent: Runners come from the `arena runners` line in the project models file, else willyskills's default, one per entry, applied with the model-entry snippet. Dropped: upstream's default slugs, the `auto`/`generalPurpose` alias handling (the snippet covers `inherit-parent`), the rejected-slug and family-prefix fallbacks with their keep-at-least-two-runners floor (it only guards seats dropped for a rejected slug), and the reasoning-level sentence, which the snippet's effort ceiling replaces. Preserve the frame steps, the more-runners and repeat-one-model guidance, and the per-candidate output location.
--- upstream
1. State the artifact each candidate is producing.
2. Derive the rubric, 3-6 concrete gradeable criteria for what success looks like on *this* task. It is the picker's tool in Phase D. Candidates only see the task.
3. Pick the runners from the `arena runners` line in `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, by default `claude-fable-5-2-high`, `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`, and `gemini-4-neon-xhigh`. An `auto` or `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model, so omit `model` and spawn `generalPurpose`. If the Task tool rejects a slug, use the nearest valid slug of the same family or drop the seat, keep at least two runners, and say so. Families go by prefix, and the longest match wins: `claude-fable-*`, `claude-*`, and `gemini-*`, after dropping a leading `cursor-`. Any other slug's family is its text before the first hyphen. Spawn more for multiple design directions, and repeat one model when the work is generation-bound, not judgment-sensitive. Pick each subagent's reasoning level per the Subagents section of the **poteto-mode** skill.
4. Give each candidate its own output location (a git worktree where possible, otherwise `/tmp/arena-<slug>/candidate-<n>/`), per the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill.
--- patched
1. State the artifact each candidate is producing.
2. Derive the rubric, 3-6 concrete gradeable criteria for what success looks like on *this* task. It is the picker's tool in Phase D. Candidates only see the task.
3. Pick the runners from the `arena runners` line in {{snippet:models-file}}, else {{model:arena runners}}, one runner per entry. {{snippet:model-entry}} Spawn more for multiple design directions, and repeat one model when the work is generation-bound, not judgment-sensitive.
4. Give each candidate its own output location (a git worktree where possible, otherwise `/tmp/arena-<slug>/candidate-<n>/`), per the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill.

=== entry ea996dc046fd
kind: translation
rules: delegate, background, isolation
intent: Fans out N candidates as N async delegate_task calls in one message, each writer in its own worktree, and ends the turn until completions wake the parent. Preserve what each brief carries: task, shared grounding path, own output path, artifact plus rationale with rejected alternatives.
--- upstream
Spawn all N subagents in one message with `run_in_background: true`, each with the task, the path to the shared grounding, its own output path, and instructions to produce the artifact and a short rationale naming the alternatives it considered and what it rejected.
--- patched
Spawn all N subagents in one message: N `delegate_task` calls with `mode: "async"`, each with its own `clientRequestId` and, when its output location is a worktree, `isolation: "worktree"`. A worktree starts from the parent's current local commit without uncommitted edits, so commit the shared grounding first or give it by absolute path. Each `task` holds the whole brief: the task, the path to the shared grounding, its own output path, and instructions to produce the artifact and a short rationale naming the alternatives it considered and what it rejected. Keep each `taskId` and `childThreadId`. Each completion wakes this thread, so end the turn instead of polling.

=== entry e0065a2510cb
kind: translation
rules: model-role, delegate, read-only, background, same-model-review
intent: The cross-judge comes from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in the project models file, else willyskills's default, and runs as a read-only async delegate_task child. A judge that picks between candidates takes the pool line as written (rule same-model-review), so the line's first entry runs the judge, and upstream's never-the-parent's-vendor check, Fable-counts-as-Claude, and the unknown-parent-model case are dropped. The rejected-slug chain is dropped except its last step: when the judge's spawn fails, skip the judge and say so, which Phase D and Outputs still refer to. Preserve that it waits for all candidates, runs alongside Phase D, and scores each candidate by path label on each criterion and recommends a base.
--- upstream
After all Phase B candidates complete, spawn one readonly judge from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, by default `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`, `gemini-4-neon-xhigh`. The judge is never from the parent's vendor, and Fable counts as Claude for that check, so use the first entry from another vendor. An `auto` or `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model. If you do not know the parent's model, use the first real slug and say that the vendor check did not run. If the Task tool rejects a slug, use the nearest valid slug of the same family, then the next such entry, or skip the judge, and say so. While you read in Phase D, the judge scores each candidate, by path label, on each rubric criterion and recommends a base.
--- patched
After all Phase B candidates complete, spawn one judge from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in {{snippet:models-file}}, else from {{model:arena cross-judge pool}}. Take the line in its configured order: its first entry runs the judge. An `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model. Spawn the judge with `delegate_task`, `mode: "async"`, and no `isolation`. Its brief says "Do not edit, create, commit, or push files.", and you run `git status` afterward. If the spawn fails, skip the judge and say so. While you read in Phase D, the judge scores each candidate, by path label, on each rubric criterion and recommends a base.

=== entry 8b5a47bda9b3
kind: translation
rules: invoke
intent: The description names both invocations, /arena for Claude Code and $arena for Codex. Everything else stays verbatim.
--- upstream
---
name: arena
description: "Spawn N parallel candidates at the same task, pick a base, graft the strongest parts of the losers into it. Use for /arena, 'arena this', 'throw it in the arena', or when one attempt at a non-trivial artifact would lock in the wrong shape."
disable-model-invocation: true
---
--- patched
---
name: arena
description: "Spawn N parallel candidates at the same task, pick a base, graft the strongest parts of the losers into it. Use for /arena or $arena, 'arena this', 'throw it in the arena', or when one attempt at a non-trivial artifact would lock in the wrong shape."
disable-model-invocation: true
---
